  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Camote and other Roots-Tubers Value Chain Improvement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main problem to be solved is the inability of producers and anchor companies to comply with the requirements of non-tariff barriers to food safety and other aspects derived from COVID-19 that are included in the quality certification standards and sustainable seals. None of the anchor companies have quality or safety certifications. The goal is to build the capacity of the personnel with whom the improvement plans are implemented, to ensure that when the certifying body carries out the inspection, they will pass the examination and obtain certification.By executing the improvement plans for the selected collection and processing plants with the participation of the personnel in charge of collection, processing, certification and field technicians, the companies are prepared to pass the certification body&apos;s examination and obtain GMP, FSMA and Global Gap certification, which will enable them to negotiate contracts and better prices with European buyers of fresh fruit.In addition, the technical and certification personnel directly in contact with the producers will receive training to transmit knowledge on the application of the Global GAP standard, which will also have an impact on producers and other crops with export potential, such as pitahaya, soursop and lemon.The project will be developed in the northern part of Nicaragua, the North Caribbean Coast, municipalities of El Rama, the department of Leon (municipality of Leon), the department of Masaya (municipality of Tisma and Masaya) and the department of Granada (municipality of Granada).</narrative>
  </description>
